  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "In Unity 1 unit is 1 metre. A model exported in centimetres arrives 100 times too big. Fix it once in the model's import settings (Scale Factor), not on each copy's Transform: then every copy starts at the right size with Scale 1, 1, 1.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> This crate looks right, but its Scale reads 0.01. You drag a second copy in from the Project window. How big will it be?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Drag Crate-cm from the Imports folder into the scene and compare.\n2. Select Crate-cm in the Project window; in the Model tab set Scale Factor to 0.01 and click Apply.\n3. Set the first crate's Scale back to 1, 1, 1.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Mesh-Shape 1 \xB7 Shapes and scale</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -6055507529455485361, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
